  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist in Kibana.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-a702a608 Web logs overview\"**\n- ID: `eff-a702a608-web-logs-overview-19af5f87e616`\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a702a608-web-logs-overview-19af5f87e616\n- Panels:\n  1. Total requests (count)\n  2. Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n  3. Requests over time (bar, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n  4. Responses by status code (pie, terms on `response.keyword`)\n  5. 5xx responses (ES|QL: `WHERE response.keyword LIKE \"5*\" | STATS COUNT(*)`)\n- Time range: last 7 days.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-a702a608 5xx spike\"**\n- ID: `d8845dc6-7e32-4771-b92c-e8efed748f63`\n- Type `.es-query`, enabled, runs every 1m, status `ok` after the first run.\n- Condition: count of documents where `response.keyword` matches `5??` in the last 5 minutes is greater than 10, grouped over all documents.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- `response` is a text field, so I matched on `response.keyword` with a `5??` wildcard rather than a numeric range.\n- The alert uses `timestamp`, the data view's time field, not `@timestamp`.\n- I did not attach any action connector, so the rule evaluates but sends no notifications. Tell me if you want one (e.g. a server-log connector).\n\nI didn't check the dashboard visually or confirm that the 5xx panel returns a non-zero count, since the ES|QL panel isn't validated server-side. The panel's query and the rule's wildcard both depend on the `response.keyword` values being three-digit status codes, which I assumed and did not verify against the index.",
